Commercial S3.2 document-reference reconciliation diagnosis
===========================================================

Observed at: 2026-08-29T16:27:40Z
Installed Application before correction:
cc1ae0e4bd961e60912311e88d394d0dbf424967

Safe symptom
------------

The retry-corrected service reached phase 18 READY with GREEN health and
NRestarts zero. It observed two queued Telegram updates and advanced its cursor
by two, but product state remained at zero submissions. The first update was an
expectedly blocked photo. The second was the explicitly selected JPEG document,
but the S3 adapter rejected it before the Application and before media storage.

The service was stopped while GREEN and the bounded window was closed. No
payment, publisher, takedown, external post or production capability ran.

Proven root cause
-----------------

Commercial S3 duplicated an older pre-download gate that required the incoming
Telegram file_unique_id to equal the previously reconciled manifest value. A
fresh upload of the same local document may carry a new Telegram reference even
when its bytes are identical. The already proven S2.2 STANDARD reconciliation
therefore validates the reference syntax, private identity, JPEG filename,
declared size and MIME type, then downloads within the exact byte limit and
binds the result by JPEG signature plus SHA-256. S3 incorrectly rejected before
that stronger content proof could execute.

Correction boundary
-------------------

S3 now follows the proven reconciliation order. A fresh Telegram reference is
accepted only when it is syntactically bounded and all other metadata matches;
the download remains capped to the manifest size and is accepted only when the
exact SHA-256 and JPEG boundaries match. The normalized internal media identity
continues to use the manifest-bound identifier.

Malformed references, non-JPEG filenames, wrong MIME type, wrong size, wrong
hash, forwarded content, photos, other media and non-allowlisted identities stay
fail-closed. Rejected ingress now emits only a safe reason code and never an ID,
filename, response body, token or media bytes.

Regression coverage proves a fresh reference with exact bytes is accepted,
unsafe metadata is rejected before download and the full local Application
suite passes 717/717.

Rollback
